WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.703
New health revelations coming to light
about Democratic Senator Dianne Feinstein.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.507
Her office confirming to our Manu Raju
that the senator suffered complications

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.309
from her long bout with shingles.

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:12.879
Complications including encephalitis,
which is an inflammation of the brain.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:17.150
Senator Feinstein this afternoon
first denied having encephalitis and said

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.051
it was just the flu.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:22.489
But her office then confirmed
that she did indeed have encephalitis.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:26.960
This is the 89 year old senator facing
is facing increasing questions

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.230
about her mental fitness and ability
to serve as a senator.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:34.434
Senator, thanks to you both.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:39.039
Senator Feinstein, do you still feel
like you're sick to some extent right now?

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:42.342
I you but you have to resign.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:45.612
Yes, you guys
women are in this sloganeering.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.113
But working for her office now

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:52.952
Thank you.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.188
I mean, it's painful to watch that.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.690
Manu Raju is OUTFRONT. Marty,
what more are you learning tonight?

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:01.628
There has not been much information
coming from Senator Feinstein

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:06.399
or her office in the aftermath of her
contracting shingles back in February.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.001
She was gone for several months.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:12.439
She returned there and she has said very
little about everything that happened.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:17.377
But then the revelation that she did get
in some flights in addition to the Ramsay

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:21.214
Hunt, syndrome, two complications
that came from the result of shingles.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:25.251
She initially denied that, said
that she was in case of the bad, bad flu.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:28.855
And then she let her office later
confirm that indeed

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.157
she had broader health complications.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.392
Then talking to senators

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:36.129
when asked about whether or not
they believe she is fit to serve.

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:37.730
They sidestepped the question

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.568
Do you have confidence that

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:44.003
she can continue to do this rigorous job?

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:48.575
We're all human
and we all have health issues.

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:53.546
And right now she is performing
as a United States senator, doing her job.

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.849
Are you worried about her abilities
to do her job?

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.651
Well, I can't answer that.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:02.989
Well, let me because I don't know why
I have confidence in her judgment

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:07.193
and her her family and her staff's
judgment

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.330
Now, questions

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.566
about Senator Feinstein
have persisted for several years.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:17.904
She was slated to become the first woman
to chair the Senate Judiciary Committee.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.974
She essentially was pushed aside
by top Democrats

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:23.977
who were concerned
about her ability to do that.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:28.081
And she could have been the first female
to be the president pro tem of the Senate,

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:29.282
meaning the most senior member

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:32.085
of the Senate, someone who's in line
in the presidential succession.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.987
She did not take that position.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:37.457
That allowed Patty Murray to become
the president pro tem instead All

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:40.860
because of these health issues that came
even before this recent bout of shingles.

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:41.394
All right, Mary,

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:42.295
what about the question

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:45.465
that we heard there in that exchange
where someone asked MS.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:48.034
Pelosi
if she was working for Feinstein's office,

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:51.538
which was referring to the woman
that has been by a Feinstein side

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:55.108
all the time, it seems recently
Nancy Pelosi's eldest daughter

00:02:55.642 --> 00:03:00.480
also seemed Also named Nancy, I should say
Nancy Careen, proud to is her name.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.816
She has been by Feinstein side
since returning to the Senate.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.853
What do you know about their relationship
Manu?

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.354
Yes, there have been.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:11.925
It was an interesting development
learning about this in recent days.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:16.696
She is someone the Pelosis
and the Feinstein have been very close

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:19.699
over the years of coming through
San Francisco politics.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:24.070
Their office says this is a personal
relationship, not a political one.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:24.971
And this is why

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.041
the former speaker's daughter, eldest
daughter,

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:32.445
is working with her, essentially working
as a caretaker of sorts.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:35.815
But it has also raised
some political questions as well.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:39.252
Nancy Pelosi is supporting Adam Schiff

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:42.989
to be the next senator from California
to replace Dianne Feinstein.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:47.860
If Feinstein were to resign,
then Gavin Newsom, the governor, has said

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.163
that he would appoint
a black woman to the post.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:54.234
If he were to do that, perhaps that could
make it shake up the Senate race there,

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:59.138
maybe make makeshift bid for
the Senate seat Senate more difficult now.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:03.009
Pelosi's office denies that's the case,
but those are

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:06.446
the questions that are swirling around
Dianne Feinstein and it'll future.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:07.614
Certainly. All right.

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.415
And adds a fascinating wrinkle to it.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.950
Manu, thank you.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.219
I want to go now to our chief
medical correspondent, Dr.

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:14.020
Sanjay Gupta.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.155
I mean, Dr. Gupta, let's just be honest.

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.057
This is something that really
has captivated the country.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.592
People want to understand
what's going on here.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.594
And obviously, you're a neurosurgeon.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:24.364
Let's just start
with this latest news on encephalitis.

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:27.467
Which they said, you know, she didn't have
and then said, in fact, she had.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:31.304
How serious could encephalitis be
and what does it do to a brain?

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.606
Well, it can be very serious.

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:36.909
I mean, it's it's inflammation
of the brain, the whole brain.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.512
I mean, people often
have heard the term meningitis.

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:41.214
And I'll just show you here quickly, Erin.

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:46.319
Meningitis is an inflammation of the outer
layers of the brain with encephalitis.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:48.054
You're talking about the brain itself.

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:51.257
And it can be a challenging diagnosis
that will tell you to make.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:55.128
They they had suspicion probably
because of her shingles initially.

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:58.031
And then she probably had symptoms,

00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:59.899
which can be a little bit vague
in the beginning.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:01.801
But things like fever,

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:04.337
it could be neck ache,
sensitivity to light,

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:07.540
but then it can go into mental confusion

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.710
and seizures and it can be, again,
a challenging diagnosis.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:13.946
You get MRI scans,
you may even have to do a lumbar puncture

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:16.983
to find out, but it can be serious.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:20.253
If it's not treated,
it can resolve as well.

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:23.356
And a lot of the sort of more acute
symptoms if you will,

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:26.592
fever and pain and things
like that, headache, they can go away.

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:31.664
But you could be left with with mental
confusion, difficulties with memory.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.399
And she's 89 years old.

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:37.036
So, you know, all of that is amplified
in someone who is that old as well, Erin.

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:37.837
No, certainly.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.907
And as you say, those things are not
the ones that necessarily go away.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.942
So these are
these are serious considerations.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:46.779
So now the senator's office is saying
while her encephalitis has resolved

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:47.413
and obviously due

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:50.750
to what you just said, we don't know
exactly what that means fully.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.652
But they also say she continues

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:56.656
to have complications from something
called Ramsay Hunt Syndrome.

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:58.791
What is Ramsay Hunt Syndrome?

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:01.561
Yeah, well,
this is another sort of consequence

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:04.731
that that rare one
but a consequence of shingles sometimes.

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:09.736
So both encephalitis and Ramsay Hunt
could be a result of her initial shingles.

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:11.304
What this is

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.306
and you may have heard of seeing
a lot of people have heard of shingles.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:15.308
Basically,
if you've had chicken pox as a kid,

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:18.678
the virus that causes
chickenpox may not go away.

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:20.113
It stays inside your body.

00:06:20.113 --> 00:06:23.216
And then at some point, as adults,
it gets reactivated.

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.985
We don't really know why.

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:28.788
And this case,
it could have been reactivated

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:31.190
for all sorts of different reasons,
but it affects that nerve.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:31.791
We just showed it.

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:33.526
There on the screen for a second.

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.161
It's the facial nerve.

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:38.564
That's the yellow sort of lines
you see on someone's face there.

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:43.636
It can affect all those nerves, people's
faces, may essentially become paralyzed

00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:44.704
as a result of that.

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:48.775
They may develop lesions even in their
ear, along their face, in their eye.

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:50.576
She was complaining about her eyes.

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:52.011
The lesions could be inside the mouth.

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:53.679
It can be really painful.

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:56.282
People who've had shingles will oftentimes
describe the pain

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:56.983
that they have with that.

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:59.585
Imagine that, Aaron, on your face.

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:03.723
Now, it can also resolve,
but it can take a while.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.458
How quickly was it diagnosed?

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:07.894
Did she get antivirals
where she given steroids?

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:10.897
Those are the types of things
that can actually make it go away.

00:07:10.897 --> 00:07:11.831
Quicker.

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:14.767
People often compare it to Bell's Palsy,
which is similar.

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:20.106
But Ramsey Hunt is often more serious
and is less likely to resolve completely

00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:23.342
Well, these things are it's
very important to understand it

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:26.579
and of course, incredibly serious
and and frightening, I'm sure.

00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:28.114
All right. Thank you very much, Sanjay.

00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:29.549
Thank you.

00:07:29.549 --> 00:07:31.083
All right.
Well, this is coming as Senator

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:34.620
Feinstein is facing growing calls
from fellow Democrats to step down.

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:37.423
So what do the voters in California think?

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:41.060
Kyung Lah is OUTFRONT in San Francisco,
which is Feinstein's hometown

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:46.833
I was mayor of San Francisco
for nine years.

00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:50.203
Senator Dianne Feinstein
conducting normal business didn't

00:07:50.203 --> 00:07:52.939
change concerns at home about her health.

00:07:53.206 --> 00:07:56.309
And anything we can do to help,
I think we should.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:59.912
After these images earlier
this week that stunned

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:03.282
San Francisco native Tom Benton
just sadness.

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:07.854
I think first and foremost, shock
to some degree at

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:11.190
at how frail she seems.

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:14.760
Benton of progressive group
Indivisible helped organize

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.364
this open letter to Senator Feinstein,
signed by activists

00:08:18.364 --> 00:08:22.568
across California asking her to
resign to focus on her health

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:26.172
Then had voted for Feinstein for decades.

00:08:26.372 --> 00:08:29.408
He'd witnessed her ascent
from the first female mayor of San

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:32.612
Francisco to the first woman
California sent to the U.S.

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:33.346
Senate.

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:37.316
A trailblazer
who Benton says needs to pass the torch.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:40.486
Why would anybody wish that on a man
